$ krowk
stdout:
█  █  Krowk 0.0.0-golden
█▀▀▄  A coding agent harness: one session, any machine, model or agent

Usage
  krowk                      Open the agent here
  krowk -p "…"               One prompt, headless
  krowk <command> [flags]

Examples
  krowk connect anthropic    Connect a model to run the agent on
  krowk push shot.png        Upload a screenshot and get a link to paste
  krowk sessions --json      Every agent session on this machine, as data

Agent
  connect       Connect a model: Claude, ChatGPT, SuperGrok or an API key
  disconnect    Sign a connected model out
  status        What's connected, and whether each is ready
  sessions      List and read agent sessions on this machine
  sync          Sync sessions between your machines, end-to-end encrypted
  devices       The machines that sync this workspace's sessions

Publish
  push          Upload files, get a link for each
  runs          Group uploads under a run
  artifacts     Create, list, show, attach, delete or claim artifacts
  claim         Keep an anonymous upload past expiry

Account
  login         Sign in to your krowk account
  logout        Remove this machine's key
  whoami        Show the key and its workspace
  workspaces    Switch between stored keys

Other
  providers     Low-level instance config (add, list, rename, remove)
  worktrees     The git worktrees krowk made for agents, across repositories
  host          The daemon sessions run in, which outlives the terminal
  config        Show or set configuration
  doctor        Check this machine's setup
  pricing       Refresh model prices
  upgrade       Upgrade krowk

Flags
  --model <instance/model>   Which model (e.g. claude/sonnet)
  --resume · --worktree      Continue a session, or start one in a worktree
  --json · --jq <expr>       Output as JSON, or filter it
  -h, --help · -v, --version

krowk help <command>  A command's own flags
krowk help --all      Every command and subcommand
krowk help topics     Flags, exit codes, environment, workspaces, links
krowk help agents     For AI agents and scripts: the output contract
exit: 0

